Subject: [PATCH] Twelve dark seats diagnosed, fred.json fixed on both halves,
 and the liveness fence

Landed on the box that runs the producers, as ONE commit rather than five, to keep
the seal green in the approach to the 05:00Z window. Full reasoning is in the five
build-box commits afd70d1, 5e5ae3a, 5027819, 96b6460, b5040af.

1. THE LIVENESS FENCE (scripts/check_organ_cadence.py, 18 tests, registered in
   run_law_gate _STATE_FENCES). Twelve seats donated nothing in 24h and five were
   not stubs -- event_response_atlas 258 artifacts then silence, graveyard_
   resurrection 220, research_tree 138, fbs_tape 82, axis_registry 45. Four of the
   five logged LEG_DONE outcome=ok EVERY HOUR while producing nothing. Three
   fences already watched this ground: check_leg_rotation asks whether a leg RAN
   (one that fails every time ATTENDED), check_seat_health asks whether a seat is
   OVERDUE (equally true of a seat with no clock and one whose donation door
   broke), and check_organ_liveness reads the VPS cron plane and on this box
   judged 0 of 0 rows and exited 0. None of them joins "it ran" to "its output
   moved". This reads the contract the desk ALREADY declares -- tier1_program.json
   scheduled_by + artifact, 352 rows nothing had ever read as one -- and separates
   the SELF channel (an organ describing its own run) from the PRODUCT channel
   (what the compiler eats). MEASURED HERE over 242 organs: 2 SILENT_NOOP, 5
   REPORTS_BUT_PRODUCES_NOTHING, 11 ALWAYS_FAILING -- including external_gauntlet
   (the JUDGE) failing 11 of 11, compile_candidates 10 of 10 and deep_forest 16 of
   16, none of which anything was watching. It also publishes the SEAL'S DUTY
   CYCLE per sleeve-day window: 8 of 21 windows in 7 days closed with a placement,
   13 closed on refusals, 742 of them release_identity_refused. Today's eighteen
   are declared by name on a list that may only SHRINK, so the gate is usable
   tonight rather than red on an inherited backlog, and the nineteenth fails on
   the day it appears.

2. FRED.JSON, BOTH HALVES. The writer was rewriting a populated axis into an empty
   one every hour, beside bis.json at 85.9 MB on the same clock: ingest_fred
   swallows every per-series exception so it never raises, the driver's except
   never fires, and the success path wrote the empty document anyway. An empty
   fetch can no longer overwrite a populated axis (EMPTY_REFUSED_OVERWRITE, with
   the count it preserved), and the write is atomic. The fetch itself was a
   User-Agent: measured back to back on this box, the desk's token draws
   ConnectionReset after 19.2 s and curl/8.4.0 draws HTTP 200 in 0.04 s. Nothing
   is bypassed -- fredgraph.csv is keyless and answers plain python-urllib -- and
   the token is scoped to FRED so the three axes ingesting 85.9 MB, 1.1 MB and
   786 KB are untouched.

3. THE GIT-WRITER REAPER. HUNG_MIN_AGE_S 1800 -> 600, HUNG_SAMPLE_S 15 -> 60. At
   1800 s on a 15-minute clock a wedge is invisible for up to 45 minutes, and one
   was: the reaper reported CLEAR five consecutive times while a push held the
   writer mutex, SealIfClean could not take the lock, and allows_new_risk stayed
   False into the approach of a placement window. The delta proof carries the
   verdict now; the floor's real job is only to clear Adopt-And-Seal's 540 s mutex
   wait, because a writer BLOCKED WAITING also burns no CPU and moves no bytes.
   The longer sample makes this strictly LESS likely to kill live work, and five
   tests cover the trigger-happy direction including a chunked push moving only
   bytes and a gc moving only CPU.

4. THREE SEATS REPAIRED, each for its own cause. event_response_atlas applied its
   OWN Bonferroni threshold as a donation filter -- a bar that RISES with
   generation: at 636 cells t=3.9486 against a best cell of t=-3.617, so it shut
   itself. RESEARCH.md 6d forbids a producer-private bar in either direction, and
   the fixed 7x DSR multiplier already prices multiplicity once, downstream.
   MEASURED: 279 of 300 cells clear cost, 0 clear Bonferroni; donations 0 -> 15.
   research_tree donated from frontier[:30], a PUBLICATION cut; MEASURED: the
   published 30 hold 0 nodes with a spec while the full frontier holds 3,292
   donatable ones; donations 0 -> 20. alpha_periodic_table's __main__ was a
   print-only demo that never called main(), so its report went 47h stale while
   the leg exited 0 hourly.

5. FIVE SEATS RETIRED WITH REASONS, and hunt17 buried. brain has NO writer
   anywhere in the tree; cohorts and scheduled_chatgpt have writers behind a dead
   import chain or no task; literature and frontier are roster misattributions
   whose work lands elsewhere. Each carries an inheritor. fbs_tape is NOT retired
   -- it is a real producer that needs a clock, and retiring a working producer
   would reduce production. hunt17 exits 1 after 1.0 s on BeyondMeat_H1.parquet, a
   single-name equity the two-lane mandate correctly removed, so the
   restart-forever supervisor has been spawning a process to die in one second for
   91 hours; its clock is withdrawn and nothing is deleted. hunt23_partial and its
   five siblings are stale CHECKPOINTS beside fresh finals, not unfinished work.

BARS ARE FIXED AND NONE MOVED: gate_spec.yaml, the ten gates and the fixed trial
count are untouched. Nothing here caps, shrinks or vetoes anything; every change
makes more reach the judge.

